                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "34525847",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198002049680",
                            "num_reviews": 31,
                            "playtime_forever": 54,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 54,
                            "last_played": 1503827723
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "After having this on my wishlist for 9 months since getting a Vive, I finally got the game once it released and was sourly disappointed. The gameplay isn't RTS, its simply spamming ships against an equally spammable opponent and choosing targets during the ensuing (and prolonged) battle. Neither the campaign nor solo skirmish battles offer any objectives, tactical incentives, terrain, or really much of anything to levy as an advantage over your opponent. The controls are clunky but manageable, the environments are aesthetic enough, and I had a good \"feel\" going into it from the menu, but the gameplay itself is lackluster at best. I can't even see playing this on the supported multiplayer as having any value over bots since there is a total lack of any strategic elements. I do not recommend this game and am extremely disappointed after having had my eye on it for months as an extremely anticipated VR space RTS.",
